          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#abstract_definition Abstract definition
          %p
            A
            %em dg-coalgebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          %p
            Equivalently, this is a graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coderivation"} coderivation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D : C \to C
          %p that is of degree -1 and squares to 0,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^2 = 0
                  \\,.
          %h3#detailed_component_definition Detailed component definition
          %h4#precoalgebra Pre-coalgebra
          %p
            A
            %em pre-graded coalgebra
            (pre-gc),
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\Delta, \varepsilon)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} pre-gvs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            together with linear maps of degree 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ε
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta: C\to C\otimes C,    \varepsilon : C\to k,
          %p
            such that the obvious (usual) diagrams commute. (When there is no ambiguity, we may write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            instead of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\Delta, \varepsilon)
          %p
            The field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a coalgebra for the canonical isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\to k\otimes k
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon = id_k
          %p
            A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : C \to C'
            of pre-gcs is a linear mapping of degree zero such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo =
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ψ
                  %mi and
                  %mi ε
                  %mo =
                  %mi ε
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi \otimes \psi)\circ \Delta = \Delta' \circ \psi   and    \varepsilon = \varepsilon' \circ \psi.
          %p
            The linear counit mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon :C \to k
            is always a morphism of pre-gcs.
          %h4#coaugmentations Coaugmentations
          %p
            A
            %em coaugmentation
            of a pre-gc is a morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : k \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(1)
          %p
            The cokernel
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            can be identified with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ker
                  %mi ε
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ker \varepsilon
            and so can be considered as a subspace of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The reduced diagonal
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta} : \bar{C} \to \bar{C}\otimes \bar{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            is defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta x = 1\otimes x + x\otimes 1 + \bar{\Delta }x
            %em vector space of primitives
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(C)
          %p
            A morphism of coaugmented pre-gcs,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : (C,\eta)\to (C',\eta')
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta' = \psi \circ \eta
          %h4#the_commutation_morphism The commutation morphism
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
            be two pre-gvs. The commutation morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau : V\otimes V' \to V'\otimes V
          %p
            is defined by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi v
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau( v\otimes v') = (-1)^{|v||v'|} v'\otimes v
          %h4#tensor_product_of_pregcs Tensor product of pre-gcs.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\Delta, \varepsilon)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ε
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C',\Delta', \varepsilon')
            be two pre-graded coalgebras. The mappings
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ′
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi τ
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\otimes C'\stackrel{\Delta\otimes \Delta'}{\to}C\otimes C\otimes C'  \otimes C'\stackrel{C\otimes \tau \otimes C}{\to}(C\otimes C')\otimes (C\otimes C')
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi ε
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ε
                      %mo ′
                  %mi k
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi k
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≅
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\otimes C'\stackrel{\varepsilon\otimes \varepsilon'}{\to}k \otimes k\stackrel{\cong}{\to}k
          %p
            give
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\otimes C'
            a pre-gc structure.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
            are coaugmentations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
            respectively, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi η
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta\otimes\eta'
            defines a coaugmentation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\otimes C'
          %h4#coderivations_of_pregraded_coalgebras Coderivations of pre-graded coalgebras
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a pre-gc, a
            %em coderivation
            of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \in Hom_p(C,C)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi C
                  %mo +
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi and
                  %mi ε
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \circ \theta = (\theta \otimes id_C + \tau \circ(\theta \otimes id_C)\circ \tau)\circ \Delta,  and  \varepsilon\circ \theta = 0.
          %p
            A coderivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            of a coaugmented pre-gc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\eta)
            is a coderivation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi η
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta\circ \eta = 0
          %h4#differential_graded_coalgebras Differential graded coalgebras
          %p
            A
            %em differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
            on a (coaugmented) pre-gc,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\circ\partial = 0
          %p
            The pair,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \partial)
            is called a
            %em differential (coaugmented) pre-graded coalgebra
            (pre-dgc). Its homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(C,\partial)
            will be a pre-gc.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C',\partial')
            are two pre-dgcs, then their tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial)\otimes(C',\partial')
            is a pre-gdgc with the structures defined earlier.
          %p
            A
            %em morphism
            of (coaugmented) pre-dgcs is a morphism both of (coaugmented) pre-gcs and of pre-dgvs. We denote the resulting categories by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pre
                  %mi DGC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre DGC
            (resp.
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pre
                    %mi η
                    %mi DGC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre \eta DGC
          %h4#cocommutative_predgcs Cocommutative pre-dgcs
          %p
            A pre-gc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %em cocommutative
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau\circ\Delta = \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pre
                  %mi CDGC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre CDGC
            (resp.
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pre
                    %mi η
                    %mi CDGC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre \eta CDGC
          %h4#cdgc CDGC
          %p
            A
            %em cocommutative differential graded coalgebra
            is a pre-cdgc on a graded vector space of lower grading (so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_p = 0
            for
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \lt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CDGC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CDGC
            (resp.
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mi CDGC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta CDGC
          %h4#connected__cdgcs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-connected
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            cdgcs
          %p
            A coaugmented cdgc
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \partial)
            is
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-connected
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}_p = 0
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\leq n
          %p
            This gives a category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CDGC
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CDGC_n
            = succeed "-connected)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}
            coinciding with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_+
          %h4#homalgebras_and_duals Hom-algebras and duals
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial)
            be a pre-cdgc and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,d)
            a pre-cdga. The pre-dgvs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Hom(C,A),D)
            is a pre-cdga for the usual differential and the multiplication
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo .
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f.g = \mu\circ (f\otimes g)\circ \Delta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi μ
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\stackrel{\Delta}{\to}C\otimes C\stackrel{(f\otimes g)}{\to}A\otimes A\stackrel{\mu}{\to} A,
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \in Hom(C,A)
          %p
            In particular
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#(C,\partial)= (Hom(C,k),D)
            defines a functor from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pre
                  %mi CDGC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre CDGC
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pre
                    %mi CDGA
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre CDGA
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %msub
                      %mi CDGC
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi CDGA
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \# CDGC_n \subseteq CDGA^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,d)
            is a pre-cdga of finite type,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#(A,d)
            is a pre-cdgc.
          %h4#coalgebra_filtrations Coalgebra filtrations
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial)
            be a pre-dgc. A
            %em coalgebra filtration
            (resp.
            = succeed ")" do
              %em differential coalgebra filtration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial)
            is a family of subspaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in \mathbb{Z}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi Δ
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊆
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi k
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi resp
                  %mo .
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ∂
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p C\subseteq F_{p+1} C, \quad \Delta F_p C \subseteq \sum_k F_k C\otimes F_{p-k} C, \quad (resp.\quad and \quad \partial F_p C\subseteq F_p C).
          %h4#filtrations_of_the_primitives Filtrations of the primitives
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\eta)
            be a coaugmented pre-gc,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}
            the cokernel of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta}
          %p
            The iteration of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta}
            is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi …
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta}^1 = \bar{\Delta}; \quad \bar{\Delta}^p = (\bar{\Delta}\otimes \bar{C} \otimes \ldots \bar{C}) \otimes \bar{\Delta}^{(p-1)}.
          %p
            The (increasing) filtration of the primitives is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ker
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p C = Ker\bar{\Delta}^p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\geq 1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\partial, \eta)
            is a coaugmented pre-dgc, each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p C
            is stable under the differential and, in particular,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1 = P(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            thus defines a functor from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pre
                  %mi η
                  %mi CDGC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre \eta CDGC
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pre
                    %mi DGVS
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pre DGVS
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            be the comultiplication of the pre-ga
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \# C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Im
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Im\bar{\mu}^p
            is the orthogonal complement of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ker
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ker\bar{\Delta}^p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo #
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo #
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\# C) =\# P(C)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\eta)
            be a coaugmented pre-gc and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p C
            the filtration of its primitives.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %em conilpotent
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi k
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \bigcup_k F_k C
          %h4#the_pregc_structure_on_
            The pre-gc structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(V)
          %p
            We will denote by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T'(V)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(V)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta}(v_1\otimes \ldots \otimes v_n) = \sum_{p=1}^{n-1} (v_1\otimes \ldots \otimes v_p)\otimes(v_{p+1}\otimes \ldots \otimes v_n).
          %p
            The counit and the coaugmentation are the natural mappings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(V)\to k
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\to T(V)
          %p
            The coalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T' (V)
            is non-commutative if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mi V
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim V\gt 1
            and has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            as its vector space of primitives.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a conilpotent pre-gc, then any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C\to V
            of pre-gvs for which
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(1) = 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f}:C \to T'(V)
          %h4#shuffles Shuffles
          %p
            A
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shuffle"} shuffle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is a permutation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1, \ldots, p+q\}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi if
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi j
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi or
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi j
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mi q
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma(i) \lt \sigma(j) \quad if \quad 1\leq i\lt j\leq p \quad or \quad p+1 \leq i \lt j\leq p+q.
          %h4#the_precgc_structure_on_
            The pre-cgc structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge V
          %p
            We will denote
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mo ′
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge' V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge V
            together with the coalgebra structure in which the reduced diagonal is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi …
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi σ
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi …
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi …
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\Delta}(v_1\wedge \ldots \wedge v_n) = \sum_{p=1}^{n-1} \sum_\sigma\varepsilon(\sigma)(v_{\sigma(1)}\wedge \ldots \wedge v_{\sigma(p)})\otimes(v_{\sigma(p+1)}\wedge \ldots \wedge v_{\sigma(n)}),
          %p
            in which the second sum is over all
            = succeed "-shuffles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,n-p)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon(\sigma)
            is the Koszul sign of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            The counit and coaugmentation are the natural mappings
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge V \to k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\to \bigwedge V
            respectively.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a conilpotent pre-cgc, any pre-gvs morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:C \to V
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(1) = 0
            admits a unique lifting to a pre-cgc morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mo ′
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f} : C \to \bigwedge' V
          %p There is an injective homomorphism of pre-gcs
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo ′
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi : \bigwedge{\!}' V \to T'(V)
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi ν
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi …
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(x_1\wedge \ldots x_n) = \sum_\nu \varepsilon(\nu)x_{\nu(1)}\otimes \ldots \otimes x_{\nu(n)},
          %p
            where the sum is over all permutations and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon(\sigma)
            is the corresponding Koszul sign. It has, as image, all the symmetric tensors (in the graded sense).
          %p
            On
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mo ′
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge' V
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T'(V)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo ′
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                  %mover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mi k
                  %mi V
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p\bigwedge{\!}' V = \bigwedge^{\leq p}V = \bigoplus_{k\leq p}\bigwedge^k V;
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p T'(V) = T^{\leq p}(V) = \bigoplus_{k\leq p} T^k(V).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %h3#differential_graded_algebras Differential graded algebras
          %p
            Dually, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          %h3#semifree_dgcoalgebras_and_algebras
            Semifree dg-coalgebras and
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            The notion of dg-coalgebra whose underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
            is cofree is related by duality to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
          %p
            Semicofree dg-coalgebras concentrated in negative degree and with differential of degree -1 are the same as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebras"} L-∞-algebras
          %h3#model_category_structure Model category structure
          %p
            There is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsFilteredColimits As filtered colimits of finite-dimensional pieces
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every dg-coalgebra is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              of its finite-dimensional sub-dg-coalgebras.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#GetzlerGoerss99"}> Getzler-Goerss 99
            ), in generalization to the analogous fact for plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebras"} coalgebras
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "coalgebra#AsFilteredColimits"} coalgebra – As filtered colimits
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "L-infinity-algebra#IndConilpotency"} Ind-Conilpotency
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+for+L-infinity+algebras"} model structures for L-infinity algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+for+L-infinity+algebras#OnProAlg"} there
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#GetzlerGoerss99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"} Paul Goerss
              = succeed "," do
                %em A model category structure for differential graded coalgebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~pgoerss/papers/model.ps"} ps
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GetzlerGoerss99.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
